  "name": "STEROID PANEL 21 HYDROXYLASE LEVEL TEST",
  "code": "1791",
  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<ul class=\"marker:text-textOff list-disc\">\n<li>\n<p class=\"my-0\"><span style=\"font-size: 11px;\"><strong>Elevated 17-Hydroxyprogesterone:</strong>&nbsp;Consistent with 21-hydroxylase deficiency (classic CAH) when confirmed by clinical context.</span></p>\n</li>\n<li style=\"font-size: 11px;\">\n<p class=\"my-0\"><span style=\"font-size: 11px;\"><strong>Low/Nondetectable Cortisol:</strong>&nbsp;Suggests adrenal insufficiency.</span></p>\n</li>\n<li style=\"font-size: 11px;\">\n<p class=\"my-0\"><span style=\"font-size: 11px;\"><strong>Abnormal Androgen Levels:</strong>&nbsp;May indicate androgen excess from adrenal origin.</span></p>\n</li>\n<li style=\"font-size: 11px;\">\n<p class=\"my-0\"><span style=\"font-size: 11px;\"><strong>ACTH Levels:</strong>&nbsp;Elevated in primary adrenal insufficiency.</span></p>\n</li>\n<li style=\"font-size: 11px;\">\n<p class=\"my-0\"><span style=\"font-size: 11px;\"><strong>21-Hydroxylase Antibody:</strong> Positive in autoimmune adrenalitis (if tested).</span></p>\n</li>\n</ul>",
